\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1c1dcd91c61bc826739daada5d6a80492d51f36770bdadf3ccd1590ab6231464","event_uuid":"b48e098a-e634-4759-9ac6-2174d904d92d","position":{"commit_sha":"efdf1ebc4713e6d6efcbf22289f96874352c5ba0","position":"1787051873443933001-b48e098a-e634-4759-9ac6-2174d904d92d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7f2c2a96a2262af4a8f67a500f39981bb6f4b0ab19fb270d8c2421cf752dbb37","event_uuid":"9d9aa4b5-8d4a-4399-ba3c-7ce39f92cff1","position":{"commit_sha":"721105692ea947fb3ec9a57bd45737c0a69bdca9","position":"1787051888084907001-9d9aa4b5-8d4a-4399-ba3c-7ce39f92cff1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Decision-register update (2026-08-17): grounding fork/callable-contract choice is RESOLVED by operator approval — spawn default, optional caller-supplied context, importable/pickleable callable contract, fail-open serialization failures, no cloudpickle/loky absent a concrete caller. Implementation is active under stumpy-cinnabar-basenji.\n\nAdded pending escalation candidate: paper-spiritous-halicore (Bedrock completion eval bulk-banks after front-loading evidence; 0/3 incremental-gap oracle in two live runs while all trials reach PASS and bank all criteria). This may be model-variance / oracle-policy rather than a product defect; hold for joint not-a-bug/design disposition unless prompt regression evidence establishes a violated contract.","timestamp":1787025865491918001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLAIM: plan-review gate bypassed by user approval — no plan-review attestation was verified. Reason: \"Operator requested this durable decision register remain active throughout the debugging sweep\".","timestamp":1787026474892597001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pending design escalation — unamicable-exuberant-chupacabra (9c90-9015-78ea-4d2c): proven runtime RCA shows the exact zero-pending gate scans all 4,371 ticket directories and cannot satisfy the authoritative 20 ms budget with any tested stateless exact reducer (best measured about 69.5 ms; current path 437–504 ms). Recommended choice: move the exact scan off the caller into a detached, coalesced gate/drain child, with bounded-spawn and lock-coalescing semantics. Alternatives: persistent derived HEAD-keyed queue index with atomicity/invalidation/rebuild policy; accept about 70 ms and raise the budget; or disable/scope opportunistic drain. No Phase 2 work or implementation exists; resume at plan/file-impact + held-out RED oracle after user decision.","timestamp":1787039761637697001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pending contract escalation — silt-resistant-gonolek (b0a8-5496-d178-40a9): raw package-free execution of private `_concurrency.py` regressed at d9e0f0e733 and now raises `ModuleNotFoundError`, but every supported production/library/subprocess route establishes `rebar_reconciler` package context before `applier._load_concurrency()` and succeeds; the caller census found no other route and canonical adapter identity is already singular. Exact decision: must every location-pinned/by-file-loaded reconciler module execute without package context, or only modules that explicitly declare and bootstrap a standalone contract? Recommendation: require context-free execution only for explicitly bootstrapped standalone modules. “Location-pinned” in ADR 0083 describes filesystem coupling, not a public entry-point promise; `_concurrency.py` is private, says it is inert on its own, and cannot be reached through applier without package context. Under this choice, classify silt-resistant-gonolek as `misunderstanding` / not-a-bug and close without code. If the operator instead wants universal context-free execution, approve that as a new package-wide contract and resume this ticket with the canonical dotted `lazy_load` repair plus an explicit contract test.","timestamp":1787051873443933001}],"created_at":1787018409098124001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d782d22b-c363-458f-adbd-28c73c0732b5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5701-5e57-2e94-4b17"},{"link_uuid":"de73492c-4df7-4a41-83e7-32d9333d1078","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1d22-40ba-8e2b-4f67"},{"link_uuid":"f33c1e22-cdcf-4409-9d2c-1a967a8c5ce8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"acf9-154e-ca76-4aac"},{"link_uuid":"9203f902-ba8c-4aaf-8554-fb0b050d197c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5b32-37c4-f99a-4315"},{"link_uuid":"0d23077f-dc95-45b1-9d4d-181ef761bee6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"adb6-4762-90f6-4e30"},{"link_uuid":"9d9aa4b5-8d4a-4399-ba3c-7ce39f92cff1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b0a8-5496-d178-40a9"}],"description":"## Purpose\nDurable register of parentless open bugs whose rebar-debug investigation reaches the not-a-bug or design-choice escalation bar. Keep unresolved decisions here so the operator can resolve them together without losing root-cause context. Each bug retains its detailed evidence and RCA on its own ticket.\n\n## Pending decisions\n- `afflicted-hexed-arthropods` — choose code-review invocation/enforcement semantics. Recommended compatible contract: explicit CLI/library/MCP `review-code` always runs by sending `enabled=True`; retain `verify.enable_code_review` only as the default for direct/internal verdict production; keep the Gerrit adapter explicit override because deployed receiver activation is already its enforcement control. Alternative: introduce a true `enforce_code_review` key, wire Gerrit voting to it, and coordinate repository plus deployed receiver configuration atomically so the currently-live LLM-Review gate is not silently disabled.\n- `peach-chemic-hairstreak` — choose the repository Bedrock default and provenance scope. Recommended: pin `us-east-1`, matching the measured provider overlay, CI defaults, service runbook, and compose defaults, and add truthful source metadata so provider provenance reports `repo-config`; keep `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION` higher precedence. Alternatives: pin `us-west-2` based on the local `frontier-bedrock` profile, or leave the repo unpinned and treat fresh-shell setup as an operator profile/env responsibility.\n\n## Resolved during sweep\n- `dragonish-sylphic-sheep` — preserve Chat Completions with `openai-chat:`; future Responses migration tracked by `upbeat-illadvised-springtail`.\n- `novel-unwasteful-stonefly` — user authorized broad typed validation, including enum and non-enum coercion, for this bug.\n- `stumpy-cinnabar-basenji` — spawn by default, optional caller-supplied context, importable/pickleable callable contract, fail-open serialization boundaries, and no cloudpickle/loky absent a concrete caller.\n- `paper-spiritous-halicore` — dense successful criterion banking satisfies the product contract; incremental-gap timing is an oracle-policy preference. Closed as `not_a_bug` after operator acceptance.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every unresolved not-a-bug or design-choice escalation from the sweep is listed with the exact decision required.\n- [ ] Each listed bug is linked with `relates_to` and holds its evidence on the source ticket.\n- [ ] Operator decisions move entries from Pending to Resolved with the chosen contract recorded.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","1d22-40ba-8e2b-4f67"],["relates_to","5701-5e57-2e94-4b17"],["relates_to","5b32-37c4-f99a-4315"],["relates_to","acf9-154e-ca76-4aac"],["relates_to","adb6-4762-90f6-4e30"],["relates_to","b0a8-5496-d178-40a9"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a1fa92b3-952b-4d0a-8cd8-e9f33f1e7e0d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["debug-sweep","decision-register"],"ticket_id":"9c72-c44a-3421-45ad","ticket_type":"task","title":"Decision register for parentless bug debug sweep","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1ebc06c9-0c1f-4f89-8662-dcc6cef9f6c7","2f32da46-2110-4fb1-98a3-6ad6d9b77f7f","a1fa92b3-952b-4d0a-8cd8-e9f33f1e7e0d","ff669441-5b9b-43b5-b6bd-3e60732dd5ed","ad57cb1a-d3ca-4903-9e58-0a96ba20eec5","9203f902-ba8c-4aaf-8554-fb0b050d197c","e50ab675-277a-43e1-967b-36d6ba035b65","0d23077f-dc95-45b1-9d4d-181ef761bee6","936816af-eb39-4917-9d9b-76277bedf6a7","cb2d6a4a-edf4-4b74-8538-ab988f1b6a41","b48e098a-e634-4759-9ac6-2174d904d92d","9d9aa4b5-8d4a-4399-ba3c-7ce39f92cff1"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787054788879945891,"uuid":"7746841e-f25e-4f2b-baa8-555d2d2b698a"}